doc: ExtPutCounterChoice: PutCounter with a comma-listed CounterType$ (up to four kinds): the resolving controller picks one kind from the list (gorge effPutCounter's counterKinds>1 arm, a Min=Max=1 "counter" KChoose over the listed kinds; the kernel poses it as a ChRemCtrKind decision, the oracle comparing the options by kind) and one counter of it is put. The resolving form (Obj the recipient) asks mid-resolution (raRemCtrAny / ChRemCtrKind); the as-enters form (Obj RefReplaced, ETB$ True) asks once the permanent is on the battlefield, as ExtEnterCtrPick does. The kinds are B's low byte, B's high byte, C's low byte and C's high byte (0 = none beyond the last), in the card's printed order. dirac/ctr_choice.go.
